# Default desktop icons.
#
# Format: Label|/path/to/App.ELF|launch argument
#   - the label may be left empty, in which case the name of the matching
#     Start-menu entry is drawn -- which is the localized one, so the desktop
#     follows the application list instead of repeating it;
#   - the launch argument is optional, and is how a Linux program gets onto
#     the desktop: give the host launcher's ELF and the "Title|command" line
#     it takes (the same pair the Start menu uses).
#
# The user's own arrangement lives in /var/System/desktop.icons and replaces
# this file wholesale when it exists.

|/Userland/com.ImplusOS.filemanager/com.ImplusOS.filemanager.ELF
|/Userland/Terminal/Terminal.ELF
|/Userland/com.ImplusOS.editor/com.ImplusOS.editor.ELF
|/Userland/Chromium/Chromium.ELF
|/Userland/FireFox/FireFox.ELF
|/Userland/com.ImplusOS.settings/com.ImplusOS.settings.ELF
